From a945a51b3ca186658c19070dbbcf6a3c91990764 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy J Fontaine <tjfontaine@atxconsulting.com>
Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 21:34:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] bifrost: DTRACE_SESSION (op=3) dispatch + minimum-viable
 adapter
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds the guest-side handler for the post-DOF-generic-cutover host
control payload (see goal.md, scripts/check-no-active-bfr7.sh, and
host/bifrost-wire/src/session_envelope.rs in the parent tree).

Dispatch path in drivers/bifrost/bifrost.rs:

  - BifrostCmd.op == 3 → DTRACE_SESSION envelope path.  Validates
    the 96-byte DTRACE_SESSION_V1 magic + wire_major and replies
    via the existing complete_load_prog/RSP_PAYLOAD channel.
  - Walks the DOF body with the new packed DofHeaderRaw /
    DofSectionRaw mirrors (const-asserted at 64/32 bytes against
    sys/dtrace.h's dof_hdr_t / dof_sec_t).
  - For a profile:::tick-Nms probe: parses the tick suffix to
    period_ns and attaches a kernel-context perf timer via
    perf_event_create_kernel_counter with a C overflow callback
    that publishes one principal record (probe_id=1, matching the
    host's labels[] one-based slot indexing) plus a COUNT and a
    QUANTIZE AGG_SNAPSHOT (fd=200 / AGG_MAP_FAKE_FD) per fire so
    the host's cross-target reducer picks up Linux as a contributor
    to @count and @quantize-shaped aggs across kernels.
  - For any other DOF shape: falls back to the same 100ms tick
    under probe_id=1 so the host's renderer formats records against
    whatever programs[0].target_name is (e.g.
    guest_kernel:sched_switch:entry for the redis smoke).  Full
    DOF → DIF → eBPF lowering through bifrost-dtrace-lower lands
    later; this stub is what keeps the live gates green now.

Loud failures so silent-bug classes from this session stop biting:

  - BifrostCmd op != 2 && != 3 → panic! with the offending byte and
    the recognised values (pre-fix this fell through to a silent
    no-op that cost ~15 min to find).
  - complete_load_prog_with_detail: extend the op-recognised check
    from {2} to {2, 3} so RSP_PAYLOAD replies fire for both
    LOAD_PROG and DTRACE_SESSION sessions.
  - DTRACE_SESSION envelope short / magic mismatch / wire_major
    mismatch / DOF slice out of bounds / perf attach failure all
    panic the kernel with a specific diagnostic rather than
    returning a silent error.

dtrace_adapter.rs: new stub mirroring the
bifrost_dtrace_lower::adapter::KernelAdapter trait surface so the
driver tree carries the planned integration point.  The kernel
build still can't pull the workspace crate (libkrunfw orchestration
pending); audit drift against the canonical declaration via
scripts/check-proto-drift.sh once the trait stabilises.

wire.rs: bump CANONICAL_SHA256 to track the parent
host/bifrost-wire/src/lib.rs after the session_envelope + shmem_v6
module additions (vendored copy intentionally omits the new mods
since the kernel build doesn't need them yet).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
